# Keep the Python project out of the Vercel upload entirely.
#
# Two reasons. First, Vercel's zero-config detection sees requirements.txt and
# tries to build a Python serverless function — that is the
# "No python entrypoint found" error this file prevents. Second, none of it is
# reachable from the static site: web/ is self-contained, and its data bundle is
# generated ahead of time by scripts/build_web_data.py and committed.
#
# The live pipeline (ESMFold + Ollama) cannot run on Vercel at all; see
# web/README.md for why and DEMO.md for how to run it locally.

src/
app/
tests/
scripts/
docs/
data/
logs/

requirements.txt
run_mvp.ps1
run_mvp.sh

*.md
LICENSE
.gitignore
